<title>FRANCE: PSA, Renault, Michelin firm.</title>
<headline>PSA, Renault, Michelin firm.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in the French car sector, PSA Peugeot Citroen, Renault SA and Michelin, rose on Monday, helped by the lira's return to the ERM, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;PSA and Renault have been helped by lira strength,&quot; said one broker. Fiat has been aggressively using the weak lira to buy market share by undercutting prices of the French carmakers. Michelin likely rose in sympathy, especially as it was considered very cheap.</p>
<p>PSA firmed 2.29 percent to 626 francs, Renault was up 1.46 percent to 118.2 and Michelin was up 2.4 percent at 264.10. The market was up one percent.  </p>
<p>Another broker said the stocks were resuming levels prior to heavy selling by a big French institution.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
